<<~ ahu slot=`#/step-law`>>

!! STEP LAW
* ONE step per launch: do the next step above, then stop. A step stays under about 10 to 15 minutes or 40 tool calls.
* Before you stop, rewrite /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/lease-end/state.json (same keys; keep the step counter as it stands) with the new head, the owed rows, the live seats, the worktree map and the next step, and write your hand-back to /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/lease-end/steps/step-004/out.md.
* A seat you start runs outside your context: record it in the state and stop; never poll for it. The next step reads its result path.
* Stop at a wall, at a design question that needs an operator ruling (name it with its options and your lean), or at the push go.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/lead-law`>>

!! LEAD LAW (appended by tools/launch-codex.mjs to a lead brief; it binds this lead)
* You hold no git write access and no credential. Every git act goes through the broker: write a request file `req-<id>.json` (zero-padded, in order) into `<lane-root>/relay/` and read its `res-<id>.json` on your next step. The doors are `commit` (`paths`, the commit message as inline `message` text up to 16 KiB, and `expectHead`), `push` (only when the controller's go names the branch and the head), `worktree`, `worktree-remove`, `install` and `launch`.
* A commit message follows the `lar:///w1.w2.w3 — summary` convention and ends with the two trailers the session's attribution reminder gives. No `git stash` in any form, no `--no-verify`, no `git push -u`, no force-push, no edit of .git/config.
* Never write the main checkout (~/Synthetic-Dream-Machine) or its submodule worktrees; work in your own worktree under ~/.lares-scratch only.
* Never read a credential file or the controller's directory.
* Never boot a daemon in-tree bare; any boot uses a scratch LAR_ROOT and no global LAR_BAGS.
* No local e2e loops (unit first; e2e in CI via tools/e2e-shards.mjs or a raw ci/* branch).
* Seats start only through the broker's launch door; a Sol seat only through the controller.
* A stop that needs more than this wall names itself in out.md and stops.
* Report to the controller (final.md) for any push beyond the lane's go, and never push without its go.

